    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d872">

                <pb facs="0942" n="656" sameAs="frus:frus1916Supp/pg656"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 341.622a/199</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Page</hi>)
                        <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1916-07-31T14:00:00+01:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">July 31, 1916, 2 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                        <lb/> [<hi rendition="#italic">Received August 1, 9.45 a.
                        m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4637. Your 3562, July 24, 7 p. m. Lord Grey informs me that telegraphic instructions have been sent to
                    Australia to release the <hi rendition="#italic">China</hi> prisoners and that
                    they will be put off as soon as can be decided upon what ship they are to
                    travel. I have also asked for detail of names, ages, status, etc., of <hi
                        rendition="#italic">China</hi> prisoners and similar information regarding
                    Leiztritz, Weinert, and Voik, removed from <hi rendition="#italic">Ausabls</hi>
                    and 
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Henry S.</hi>
                     and am promised this information [as] soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Page</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
